course: dictionary
lesson: 3970
title: Fuzz: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The words around a word, its context, show you which meaning is right. «Fuzz» is a good example. Look for the clues before you choose a meaning.
explain: Most often fuzz is soft, short, light hair or fibres, like on a peach or a baby duck. «Grow a bean in a glass jar and you will see fine white fuzz near the root tip.» The clues are fine, white and root, so the fuzz is soft, fine hairs.
explain: Fuzz can also be a blurred or crackly sound or picture, as in «fuzz on the screen». «The green or blue fuzz on top» of old bread is a growth made of threads, not a sound. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: Fuzz (noun) means soft, short, light hair or fibres, like on a peach.
fact: Fuzz (noun) can mean a blurred or crackly sound or picture: «fuzz on the screen».
fact: In music, fuzz is a buzzing, distorted sound.
fact: In old slang, the fuzz means the police.
fact: Fuzz can also be a verb: fuzzes, fuzzed, fuzzing.
exercise: «Grow a bean in a glass jar and you will see fine white fuzz near the root tip.» In this sentence, what is fuzz? | *Soft, fine hairs on the root | A loud buzzing noise | The police | A blurred picture on a screen
exercise: Dad says, «The picture is all fuzz, I can't see the match.» What does fuzz mean here? | A kind of bread | *A blurred, crackly picture | Soft hair like on a duckling | A bright, shiny light
exercise: In an old film, a character shouts, «Run, the fuzz are coming!» What does fuzz mean? | A blurred picture | Soft hair | A tiny bee | *The police
test: Jade says «peach fuzz». What does she mean? | A loud crackling sound | *Soft, light hair on a peach | A sticky juice | A dark shadow
test: A guitar makes a buzzing, distorted sound called fuzz. What is fuzz here? | A bright picture | *A buzzing, distorted sound | Soft hair | The police
exam: Ella says fuzz always means soft hair. Is she right? | Yes, but only on peaches | *No, it also means a blurred sound or picture, and in old slang the police | No, fuzz can also mean a blurred or crackly sound or picture | Yes, fuzz always means soft hair and nothing else
